===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|14th century}} To [[deliver]], especially in context of [[sin]] or relevant penalties.
# To pay a price to set someone free from [[captivity]] or [[punishment]].
#: {{usex|en|to '''ransom''' prisoners from an enemy}}
# To [[exact]] a ransom for, or a payment on.
#: {{usex|en|Such lands as he had rule of he '''ransomed''' them so grievously, and would tax the men two or three times in a year.}} {{rfdatek|en|Berners}}.

